6. Recommended Separation of Responsibilities

A useful rule for this design is:

State Store = what we know / current business state
Kafka Topic = what needs to happen

This suggests a hybrid model:

PWSSP_PDM_PUBLIC
        |
        v
Kafka Streams
        |
        +--> Dedupe State Store
        |
        +--> Advice/Aggregation State Store if needed
        |
        v
PCSS_LOOKUP_REQUEST
        |
        v
PCSS Worker
        |
        v
PCSS_RESULT
        |
        v
Kafka Streams finalization
        |
        v
PANTS_PROCESSED

State stores remain extremely useful for:

source-event deduplication;

tracking completion of multiple lookups for one advice;

aggregation;

storing deterministic business state.

Kafka topics remain better suited for:

pending external work;

retryable work;

durable handoff between stages;

backlog management;

independent scaling.

